/// Specifies the default server-side encryption configuration. General
/// purpose buckets - If you're specifying a customer managed KMS key, we
/// recommend using a fully qualified KMS key ARN. If you use a KMS key
/// alias instead, then KMS resolves the key within the requester’s
/// account. This behavior can result in data that's encrypted with a KMS
/// key that belongs to the requester, and not the bucket owner. Directory
/// buckets - When you specify an KMS customer managed key for encryption in
/// your directory bucket, only use the key ID or key ARN. The key alias
/// format of the KMS key isn't supported.
pub struct ServerSideEncryptionRule {
  /// Specifies the default server-side encryption to apply to new objects in
  /// the bucket. If a PUT Object request doesn't specify any server-side
  /// encryption, this default encryption will be applied.
